<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="Learn how B&S Painting Inc. handles estimate requests, project addresses, website data, and privacy requests.">
  <section class="section">
    <article class="legal-copy">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>Effective <time datetime="2026-11-23">November 23, 2026</time></p>
      <p>This policy describes how B&amp;S Painting Inc. handles information when you use our website or contact us about a painting project.</p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>Our estimate form asks for your name, phone number, email address, the painting service you need, and the project address, including the street address, city, and ZIP code. We also receive any details you choose to provide when you call or email us. Our hosting providers may process technical information such as your IP address, browser type, pages requested, and request timestamps to deliver and secure the website.</p>

      <h2>How we use your information</h2>
      <p>We use your contact information to respond to your inquiry and coordinate your estimate. We use the project address to check our service area, plan a site visit, and prepare a quote. If you hire us, we may also use these details to schedule and perform the work, communicate about the project, and maintain business records.</p>

      <h2>Who may receive it</h2>
      <p>Our staff and crew may receive details needed to handle your request or project. Hosting, communications, scheduling, and business software providers may process information when they support those activities. We may also disclose information when required by law or to protect our legal rights.</p>

      <h2>Future analytics and advertising</h2>
      <p>We may add Meta Pixel or similar tools to measure ad performance and, depending on the settings, show relevant ads. These tools may use cookies or similar identifiers and share information such as pages visited, button clicks, browser or device identifiers, and whether a request was submitted. Project addresses and the contents of estimate form fields are for handling your request and are excluded from advertising events.</p>
      <p>Before enabling these tools, we’ll update this policy to describe the tracking we use and provide any required consent or opt-out controls. The current website has no advertising pixel and takes no separate action in response to Do Not Track signals. Where required, we’ll honor Global Privacy Control for covered advertising activity when that activity is enabled.</p>

      <h2>Future AI-assisted tools</h2>
      <p>We may use AI-assisted tools to help organize inquiries, summarize project details, or draft replies. If we use a provider for these tasks, it may process the information needed for that task. We’ll update this policy if that use materially changes how we handle personal information.</p>

      <h2>Retention and your choices</h2>
      <p>We retain information as needed to handle your request or project, maintain business records, resolve disputes, and meet legal obligations. To ask for access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal information, email <a href="mailto:Bryana@bspaintinc.com">Bryana@bspaintinc.com</a> or call <a href="tel:+19168689188">(916) 868-9188</a>. We may need to verify your identity before responding. Additional rights may apply under California law. Please avoid including unnecessary personal information in your request.</p>

      <h2>Policy updates</h2>
      <p>We’ll post changes on this page and update the effective date. When required, we’ll provide additional notice of material changes.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Base>
